<ProductLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} ogImage="/images/uploads/2025/08/IMG_0274-768x768.jpg" gallery={gallery} category={category} descriptionHtml={`<article class="cpt-single-product post-353 product type-product status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry product_category-choline-chloride" id="post-353" itemscope="" itemtype="https://schema.org/Product"><section class="product-description entry-content"><h2>Product Description</h2><div itemprop="description"><p><strong>Also known as:</strong> Choline Chloride 60% Corn Cob, 2-Hydroxy-N, N, N-Trimethylethanaminium Chloride, CC60, <a href="/product/" title="Feed additives">Feed</a>-Grade Choline Chloride.<br/><strong>Abbreviations / Trade Names:</strong> Choline Chloride 60% (Corn Cob Carrier), CC 60%, <a href="/product_category/vitamins/" title="vitamins">Vitamin</a> B4 in the feed industry.</p><hr/><h2>Choline Chloride 60% Product Overview</h2><p>Choline Chloride 60% on corn cob carrier is a <strong>high-quality, feed-grade vitamin supplement</strong> widely used in poultry, swine, ruminants, aquaculture, and pets. As an essential <strong>B-complex vitamin (Vitamin B4)</strong>, choline plays a vital role in <strong>fat metabolism, liver protection, reproductive performance, growth promotion, and feed efficiency</strong>.</p><p>Compared with lower concentrations (such as 50%), <strong>Choline Chloride 60%</strong> provides <strong>higher active choline per unit weight</strong>, improving cost efficiency in feed formulation, transport, and storage. This makes it ideal for <strong>feed mills, premix producers, and integrated farming operations</strong>.</p><hr/><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Category</strong></th><th><strong>Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Synonyms</td><td>2-Hydroxy-N, N, N-Trimethylethanaminium Chloride</td></tr><tr><td>CAS No.</td><td>67-48-1</td></tr><tr><td>Molecular Formula</td><td>[HOCH₂CH₂(CH₃)₃N]Cl</td></tr><tr><td>Molecular Weight</td><td>139.63 g/mol</td></tr><tr><td>Appearance</td><td>Free-flowing, light brown granules</td></tr><tr><td>Odor</td><td>Slight amine odor</td></tr><tr><td>Carrier</td><td>Corn cob</td></tr><tr><td>Choline Chloride Content</td><td>≥ 60% (≈ 52% pure choline base)</td></tr><tr><td>Loss on Drying</td><td>≤ 2.0%</td></tr><tr><td>Trimethylamine (TMA)</td><td>≤ 300 ppm</td></tr><tr><td>Apparent Density</td><td>~500 kg/m³</td></tr><tr><td>Particle Size</td><td>≥ 95% through 20-mesh sieve</td></tr><tr><td>Shelf Life</td><td>18 months (cool, dry storage at ≤ 25°C)</td></tr><tr><td>Packaging Options</td><td>25 kg kraft bag + PE liner / 625 kg jumbo bag / customized options</td></tr></tbody></table><hr/><h2>Key Features &amp; Benefits</h2><ul><li><strong>High Active Choline Content as Feed Additives</strong>: Ensures efficient formulation with reduced inclusion rates.</li><li><strong>Cost Efficiency</strong>: Lower transport &amp; storage cost per unit of active ingredient.</li><li><strong>Feed Performance</strong>: Prevents fatty liver, improves growth rate, fertility, egg yield, and feed conversion ratio.</li><li><strong>Ease of Handling</strong>: Free-flowing granules, excellent for premixes and direct feed blending.</li><li><strong>Regulatory Compliance</strong>: Produced under <strong>ISO 9001, FAMI-QS, and GB/T standards</strong> for international feed additive trade.</li><li><strong>Flexible Supply Chain</strong>: Multiple packaging formats for both small-scale and bulk buyers.</li></ul><hr/><h2>Application by Animal Species</h2><ul><li><strong>Poultry</strong>: Supports growth, egg production, hatchability, and FCR (feed conversion ratio).</li><li><strong>Swine</strong>: Enhances growth rate, prevents perosis, and increases litter size.</li><li><strong>Ruminants</strong>: Improves milk yield, reduces ketosis, and protects liver function.</li><li><strong>Aquaculture</strong>: Boosts growth, improves survival, and enhances feed efficiency in fish and shrimp.</li><li><strong>Pets</strong>: Promotes metabolism, liver health, and skin condition.</li></ul><hr/><h2>Usage Recommendations</h2><ul><li>Incorporate directly into <strong>premixes, compound feed, or concentrates</strong>.</li><li>Dosage depends on <strong>species, growth stage, and production goals</strong>.</li><li>Consultation with a <strong>professional feed nutritionist</strong> is strongly recommended for precise inclusion rates.</li></ul><hr/><h2>Why Choose Our Choline Chloride 60%?</h2><ul><li><strong>Manufacturer Advantage</strong>: Direct supply from China with competitive pricing.</li><li><strong>Strict Quality Control</strong>: Stable choline content, low TMA, and consistent granule size.</li><li><strong>Export Reliability</strong>: Proven logistics, bulk supply capacity, and global compliance certificates.</li><li><strong>Technical Support</strong>: Professional guidance for feed mills and integrators.</li></ul><hr/><p><strong>References for Extended Information</strong></p><ul><li>FAO/WHO JECFA specification on Choline Chloride feed additive.</li><li>National Feed Additive Standards of China (GB/T 7300 series).</li><li>EFSA Panel on Additives and Products or Substances used in Animal Feed (2011).</li><li>Scientific literature on choline metabolism and animal performance.</li></ul></div></section><section class="related-products"><h2>Related Products</h2><div class="related-products-grid"><div class="related-product-item">
